{"additions":2617,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nA new read-only **Worktrees view** (key `7`, `page:worktrees`): git worktrees and stashes side by side, with a preview pane that shows the HEAD commit of the selected worktree or the patch of the selected stash rendered with the existing side-by-side diff view.\n\n![worktrees demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/td72/vig/feat/worktrees-view/assets/demo-worktrees.gif)\n\nCloses #103, closes #104, closes #105, closes #106, closes #107\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Page skeleton (#104)** — `src/worktrees/{mod,page,state}.rs`, `page \"worktrees\"` block in `assets/default.kdl` (left column: worktrees over stashes; right: preview; `tabs` + two `bind`s onto the preview), `Config::worktrees_page()` with validation and a loader test, page registered in `main.rs`, header / status bar renderers.\n- **Worktrees pane (#105)** — `git worktree list --porcelain` parsed into `Worktree` (path shown relative to the main worktree, branch or `(detached abc1234)`, `[main]` `[locked]` `[prunable]` `[bare]` flags). The worktree vig runs in is marked `*` in green (canonical path comparison). `/` searches path + branch. Selecting a worktree shows its HEAD commit in the preview.\n- **Stashes pane (#106)** — `git stash list --format=…` parsed into `Stash` (`stash@{n}`, branch from the `WIP on` / `On` prefix, message, relative time). `/` searches message + branch. Selecting a stash shows its diff.\n- **Preview pane (#107)** — worktree: `git show --stat --first-parent HEAD` run in that worktree (hash, author, date, subject, changed files with coloured `+`/`-` bars). Stash: `git stash show -p --include-untracked stash@{n}` (falls back to no `--include-untracked` on old git), parsed with `git2::Diff::from_buffer` and fed to the Git page's `DiffViewPane` — syntax highlighting, search, Normal / Visual mode and yank work as on the Git view. `[` / `]` step through the files of a multi-file stash; the pane title shows `stash@{n}: path [i/n]`.\n- Lists reload on `r`, on fs change and when the page is activated (`git worktree add/remove` only touches `.git/worktrees`, which the watcher ignores). The preview is only re-fetched when the selected item's identity (path@HEAD / stash hash) changes.\n- Small hooks in shared code so the widget could be reused rather than re-implemented: `files_from_diff()` split out of `parse_diff()` (`src/git/domain/diff.rs`), a `title` field on `DiffViewPane`, and `execute_diff_scroll` made `pub(crate)`.\n- Docs: README (en / ja) feature bullet, view-switching row and a \"Worktrees View\" section; `docs/config.md` page / actions tables.\n- Demo: `tape/demo-worktrees.tape` + `assets/demo-worktrees.gif`, `mise run demo:worktrees` (also in `demo:all`).\n- Tests: porcelain / stash-list / `git show` parsing, current-worktree detection (including a symlinked root), display-path computation, patch-buffer → side-by-side conversion, stash row layout, KDL wiring (ids, bindings, keys, `7`), and a smoke test that builds the page for vig's own repository.\n\nRead-only by construction: the only git commands are `worktree list`, `stash list`, `stash show -p` and `show`.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Bare and prunable worktree entries are covered by parser fixtures only; not exercised against a real bare repository.\n- The `--include-untracked` fallback path (git < 2.32) was not run against an old git binary.\n- Behaviour on Windows paths (drive prefixes in `display_path`) is untested.\n- The header numbers pages by their position in the page list, so with only this page merged it reads `4:Worktrees` while the switch key is `7` (as specified); the numbering lines up once the Docker / Procs / Actions pages exist.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":26,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-28T07:51:26Z","deletions":9,"headRefName":"feat/worktrees-view","labels":[],"number":110,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPKR6w","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe preview pane currently routes key input through its own keymap even in stash diff Normal/Visual mode, preventing DiffViewPane’s vim-style key handling (v/V/y/Esc/motions) from working as intended.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a new read-only **Worktrees view** page to vig, listing git worktrees and stashes side-by-side with a right-hand preview (worktree HEAD summary or stash patch rendered via the existing side-by-side diff widget).\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces `worktrees` page wiring (KDL layout, key bindings, page registration, header/status rendering).\n- Implements worktree/stash listing + parsing and preview fetching (`git worktree list --porcelain`, `git stash list`, `git show`, `git stash show -p`).\n- Reuses Git page diff view by extracting `files_from_diff`, making diff scroll execution reusable, and allowing a configurable diff pane title.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-worktrees.tape | Adds a VHS tape to demo the new Worktrees view behavior. |\r\n| src/worktrees/state.rs | Worktrees page state: pane wiring, reload/sync logic, key handling, tests. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/worktrees.rs | Worktrees list pane UI + navigation/search actions. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/stashes.rs | Stashes list pane UI + navigation/search actions and layout helper. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/preview.rs | Preview pane rendering (HEAD summary / stash diff) and actions. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/mod.rs | Shared string fitting utilities for the Worktrees panes + tests. |\r\n| src/worktrees/page.rs | Page constructor for the new Worktrees page. |\r\n| src/worktrees/mod.rs | Registers the new worktrees module structure. |\r\n| src/worktrees/domain/worktree.rs | Worktree porcelain parsing, display path logic, and `git show` parsing + tests. |\r\n| src/worktrees/domain/types.rs | Domain types for worktrees/stashes/commit summary. |\r\n| src/worktrees/domain/stash.rs | Stash list parsing and stash patch-to-diff conversion + tests. |\r\n| src/worktrees/domain/mod.rs | Shared `git_output` helper for the worktrees domain. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Registers and instantiates the Worktrees page in the app’s page list. |\r\n| src/git/panes/diff_view/view.rs | Uses `DiffViewPane.title` instead of hardcoded `\"Diff\"`. |\r\n| src/git/panes/diff_view/mod.rs | Adds `title` to `DiffViewPane` for reuse outside the Git page. |\r\n| src/git/panes/diff_view/keys.rs | Exposes `execute_diff_scroll` within the crate for reuse. |\r\n| src/git/domain/diff.rs | Extracts `files_from_diff()` so diffs can be built from buffers too. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Adds Worktrees page header/status bar renderers. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Loads/validates the new `worktrees` page config + updates tests/app keymap pages list. |\r\n| src/core/app.rs | Extends app key switching tests to include the new page. |\r\n| README.md | Documents the new Worktrees view, keybindings, and adds it to the feature list. |\r\n| mise.toml | Adds `demo:worktrees` task and includes it in `demo:all`. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese documentation updates for the new Worktrees view and keybindings. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Extends config documentation to include the `worktrees` page and actions. |\r\n| assets/demo-worktrees.gif | Adds the recorded demo GIF (via Git LFS pointer). |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds default app binding (`7`) and full `page \"worktrees\"` layout/keys/binds. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 26/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T07:57:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"23a83ed56c3810d6df824d39b67fe7f98e329dee"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLParpQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"82a11b1420c24bb9ae59d30b3be48c5a9a69e956"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPasfg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"82a11b1420c24bb9ae59d30b3be48c5a9a69e956"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPdK9w","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe stash preview fallback currently retries without `--include-untracked` on any error, which can silently drop untracked changes from the preview instead of surfacing real failures.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 26/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:35:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"82a11b1420c24bb9ae59d30b3be48c5a9a69e956"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPfN0Q","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe preview stash path unnecessarily clones potentially large diff data (and there’s a small help-binding convention mismatch), so a quick fix is needed before approval.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**src/worktrees/panes/preview.rs:181**\n* `set_stash` clones the entire `Vec<FileDiff>` just to keep a copy in `Content::Stash` (`Rc::new(files.clone())`). For large stash patches this doubles memory and work. You can avoid the clone by letting `set_diff_files` install the `Rc<Vec<FileDiff>>` into `self.diff` and then reusing that `Rc` for the `Content::Stash` field.\n```\n        self.content = Content::Stash {\n            name,\n            files: Rc::new(files.clone()),\n            error,\n        };\n```\n**src/worktrees/state.rs:296**\n* Help bindings use an ellipsis range (\"1 … 7\"), which is inconsistent with the established convention used by other pages (explicit \"1 / 2 / 3 ...\" lists) and can be misleading since key \"6\" is not listed/used. Prefer listing the actual switch keys explicitly for consistency and clarity.\n```\n        let mut entries = vec![s(\"1 … 7\", \"Switch view\")];\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 26/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:40:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"54a6a5b988afc116b86cc9d96863f1a55d8dd1fb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPfpZQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:41:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"54a6a5b988afc116b86cc9d96863f1a55d8dd1fb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPfqRw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:41:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"54a6a5b988afc116b86cc9d96863f1a55d8dd1fb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPfrFw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:41:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"54a6a5b988afc116b86cc9d96863f1a55d8dd1fb"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:55Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156235427/job/98799555542","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:56Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:37:56Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025668/job/98798879920","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:37:05Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025646/job/98798879571","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:37:53Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025668/job/98798879731","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:35Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025668/job/98798879927","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:44Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:35Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025668/job/98799484318","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:36Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:55Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156235427/job/98799554848","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:55Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:37:24Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025646/job/98798879792","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:37:58Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156025646/job/98798879740","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:44Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:39:55Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33156235427/job/98799581957","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:40:03Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Worktrees view: worktrees, stashes and diff preview"}
